      "hints": [
        "Integrate $2x^2 - 7 - 4x^{-2}$ using the power rule.",
        "Substitute $x = 1$ and $y = -\\frac{1}{3}$ to find $c = 2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Integrate $f'(x) = 2x^2 - 7 - 4x^{-2}$ term-by-term with respect to $x$, including constant $c$:\n$$f(x) = \\int \\left(2x^2 - 7 - 4x^{-2}\\right)\\,dx = \\frac{2}{3}x^3 - 7x + 4x^{-1} + c$$",
        "Substitute the point $(1, -\\frac{1}{3})$ to solve for $c$:\n$$-\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{2}{3}(1)^3 - 7(1) + \\frac{4}{1} + c = \\frac{2}{3} - 3 + c = -\\frac{7}{3} + c$$",
        "Solve for $c$:\n$$c = -\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{7}{3} = \\frac{6}{3} = 2$$",
        "State the complete formula for $f(x)$:\n$$f(x) = \\frac{2}{3}x^3 - 7x + 4x^{-1} + 2$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
